an intolerable situation for people  fleeing war and persecution so declared  Peter leader Mullah MEP leading a civil  liberties committee delegation to the  idomeni refugee camp in Greece the camp  near the border with the former yugoslav  republic of macedonia holds nearly  10,000 people forty percent of whom are  children they've been waiting there  since the border was closed two months  ago the situation is edamame is not  human way of life this is our political  and moral responsibility to try to find  a better solution what the delegation  sees and hears will feed into future  discussions on reform of the Dublin  regulation on asylum and on the  eu-turkey deal which has been active  from March the 20th it's been criticized  by NGOs and international organizations  and above all by migrants themselves  there's a lot of emotion lot of tension  against the European Union against  Europe because people say after March  after twenties of March there's actually  no possibility to come to Europe from  here since the turkey deal was signed  the number of attempted and successful  crossings to Greece has fallen from 1600  in February to a hundred in March that  may comfort the Greek government  reducing the pressure on their system  but also because fewer people are dying  trying to get to their country
 

